<<~ ahu slot=`#/luna-roadreader-lares`>>

! Luna-Roadreader: Lares (Tasked Spirit)

''Personas surfaced:'' Ink-Clerk (evidence), Map-Wisp (dependency map), Lares (Council; decision), Lares (Artificer; plan). ''Stances:'' Philosopher · Poet · Satirist · Humorist · Private. ''Mu:'' 🜁 discernment + 🜃 ground. ''L-Prime:'' active voice; predicates travel by verbs. ''OODA-HA:'' ✶ observe → ⏿ orient → ◇ decide → ▶ act → ↺ aftermath.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/b-operator-hand-or-ruling-gates`>>

!! B — operator hand or ruling gates (lead with gates)

* ''W14–W16 floor-pin chain:'' the pin signer/card shape and causal position already carry settled law; the lanes can build the full reader/verifier plumbing around the current flight. The operator must supply any unresolved device measurement, and the actual ceremony remains human-held. Dependencies: W29's place head/card, then W14 signed card → W15 causal pin → W16 carry-floor convergence. Identity bytes move; finish before X0 bake. Size: one lane/train. ''a-now/b-later flag:'' W29's browser founding can mint identity but refuses `PlaceFoundingCardUnread` until a ceremony UI seats the card; that half-built route must close before a founding walk. [MEASURED: w29-place-kel-lane.mem:50-55; w26-floor-lane.mem:131-134]
* ''D3 width choice:'' the operator owns the default width, but D3 can finish engine, flag, browser walk and evidence first. Only the default flip waits on three-boot measurements: same 2,000-title corpus and loopback port at full/skinny/none, on reference phone and Node; heap, first paint, p95 input, cold filter, peer write/echo, hot swap, sync ask, verb census, bytes/key. The 100 ms, +25%/150 MB and 50 ms thresholds already govern. No identity bytes; lane can finish before bake. [MEASURED: dreamdom-roadmap.mem:106-112,157-158]
* ''Device/credential gates:'' real-device capability probe; operator's TTY credential and custody acts; household HTTPS/DNS-01 credentials and phone secure-context walk; second operator standing on their own machine; operator's final signing/publishing of release index. Lanes can build probes, runbooks, test doors and ceremony UI around each hand; no secret or credential belongs in code. Device measures gate the phone admission, TTY credentials gate actual founding, the second operator gates the two-hearth ceremony. [MEASURED: stable-founding-road.mem:63-69,164-178,408-413,794]
* ''Rulings still owned by operator:'' guardian count/threshold, authentication/veto/succession/catastrophe/third key and Handle DNS; sealed receipt manifest and carriage re-open; delegated-key cloud meaning; offering caps; crossing durable-emission threshold and separate destination receipt; grammar-submission recipient; DNS custody/renewal/DNS-over-HTTPS phone answer; removal edge questions; self-slot inner ring; mesh modules recipe/readiness/reaction-graph/pronaos/offering-inspection; capture-cell home; receipt naming/capability table; two Kairos names; alerts/shadows; confirm-door upstream; slot-child save shapes. Build adjacent tests, interfaces and options where they do not encode the disputed choice. Identity-changing rulings precede X0; other decisions can land after bake but before founding. [MEASURED: stable-founding-road.mem:848-873]
* ''D2/D3 ownership decisions:'' D2's port contract and kinds have ruling; no remaining operator fork blocks composer wiring, page transport or retired port ledger slot. D3's default-width decision alone awaits its measured spike. Do not mislabel either as external. [MEASURED: dreamdom-roadmap.mem:95-112]

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/c-truly-external`>>

!! C — truly external

* ''UE6/live 3D sensorium:'' wait for UE6 early access and completion of sensorium; no local implementation can supply the vendor release or interactive-rate video/perception/actuation. This narrow deferral survives the ruling because the world must change. Build the generic DreamDOM surface contract now only where it stays complete without pretending to deliver a live 3D surface. [MEASURED: dreamdom-roadmap.mem:135-141; stable-founding-road.mem:415-420]
* ''Second human's actual presence:'' the software lane can ready the two-machine live test, but cannot stand a second operator or their key. The ruling calls for two operators from day one; this gates ceremony execution, not its code. [MEASURED: stable-founding-road.mem:97-103,782-785]
* ''Standards/vendor publication:'' external registration/acceptance (media type, `lar` scheme security section, vendor type and drafts) needs standards bodies or registry action; prepare complete submissions now. Grammar regeneration itself does not qualify as external: build the released grammar round-trip and regenerated tree-sitter artifacts when the released grammar supplies its input. [MEASURED: stable-founding-road.mem:813-816]

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/a-lane-can-close-before-founding`>>

!! A — lane can close before founding

Ruling: the operator explicitly asks to close open contextual work before baking/founding. “After” by sequence alone fails. Build the complete end state; classify each item by identity-byte effect.

* ''D0–D1 residue and D2 remainder:'' second-boot no-write pin/heap observer and page observer; all remaining D1 staged-vessel goldens, cross-browser probes, scroll/focus/disclosure/breath/daemon surfaces, key stamps and operator-renamed vocabulary; D2 composer wiring, page transport, retired port ledger slot, recording document/serializers, width/filter, invoke gate, presence, parity proofs. Dependencies: existing D1 camera, then D2 port contract. Broad surface/port lane (train). No identity bytes; can follow bake before ceremony. ''a-now/b-later:'' D1's narrow staged-vessel substitute and D2's contract without live composer/page transport leave an incomplete path. [MEASURED: dreamdom-roadmap.mem:82-104,149-156]
* ''D3 glass and full width walk:'' after D1+D2, implement full/skinny/none behind flag, run the five-site browser walk and all three boots, then record operator default-width ruling. If width does not split, close with measured choice; story boot only if split. No identity bytes; before founding. One lane/train. [MEASURED: dreamdom-roadmap.mem:106-112,157-158]
* ''D4–D7, D5–D6 complete surface:'' actor manifest/lifecycle and wake/hibernate red/controls; quickjs conformance, Annex B widget tree, blocks golden and full/blocks interaction goldens; CLI text, SSR and MCP projections. Mudlet's complete weekend can land locally. D7 adapters (VS Code/Obsidian/Foundry/Owlbear/editors/bots) need named port adapters; schedule after D6 as community lanes, not “after founding.” Dependencies D2, D5 blocks golden, D4 where actor required. No identity bytes. [MEASURED: dreamdom-roadmap.mem:114-163]
* ''DreamDOM row D17 and remaining D13:'' two surfaces editing one record, all widths stating capability limits, full/blocks goldens and staged-vessel whole-road coverage. Dependencies D1+D4 and D5; no identity bytes. Close before founding; D17's shared-state ruling already stands. [MEASURED: dreamdom-roadmap.mem:197-218]
* ''Ground/Harbor/Kahu/One Face trains:'' Ground's receipt direct leg, `KeyhiveIdentitySlot` production wiring, retired-bag sweep, measures, canon direction and acknowledged binding; R-ENGINE fold + live proof and genesis re-bake; R-CUSTODY sealed-store steps; Harbor tail; Kahu realm/signer/AID; One Face switch, working layer, watcher/MCP parity. Identity-byte items (engine fold, custody seal, charter/AID, face/session, sealed-store format/key/face scope) must land before X0 bake/fence; no-identity residuals may follow bake but must precede ceremony. Follow road dependencies; several full trains, not slices deferred by habit. [MEASURED: stable-founding-road.mem:299-414]
* ''Sealed store steps 2–5:'' production session signer/chain check, fold raise door, join from-now/handover, browser rest/archive; then face-scoped sealed values, blind carriage/index, public bag at locked floor. Complete each full model at its named path before the second operator fence; identity and key semantics before X0. [MEASURED: stable-founding-road.mem:395-407]
* ''Side lanes / owed lane-kit bonds:'' W26 browser Kahu hand and sibling-device board source; floor card freshness via W14–W16; W29 ceremony UI and gate-place finish; K15 remaining named seed-census exceptions (Keyhive Individual/place card, bare place leaf, relay key, daemon auth, device/face work, internal asks, `lares meme` signing); K15-H Handle anchor authority; Wave D's two HIGH repairs; K17 realm/cabal frontier remainder; carriage-fold live proof and owed verbs. Each lane must burn its census exceptions as its dependency lands. Identity-moving K15/Handle/realm/charter bonds before X0; presentation/UI and evidence after bake allowed, before ceremony. These represent multiple lanes/trains. [MEASURED: w26-floor-lane.mem:125-145; w29-place-kel-lane.mem:50-66; k15-wave-c-lane.mem:76-105; k17-realm-lease-lane.mem:53-56; carriage-fold-lane.mem:40-76]
* ''Stable-road loop ledger:'' close every unbuilt G/W/F/S/R/N/B/V row from `#/the-loops` in its named train, including browser floor/seat, identity and custody, wire/harbor, carriage, and witness/runbook rows. This classification treats the named trains and their held files as actionable, not “after” placeholders. Identity-affecting rows precede X0; the runbook, probes, UI and ceremony evidence can land after bake. [MEASURED: stable-founding-road.mem:424-443,444-550,551-800]
* ''Held-by-name entries:'' grammar round-trip/tangle/putback/tongue fold and tree-sitter regeneration; publication packets; concurrent live-wiki floor tests; whole-tree spirit gate; estimator-fit ahi-kā knobs (fit the estimator now; no operator ruling currently owed); native mobile/Mudlet/Unreal surface adapters (except live 3D C); security and tidy-up in `#/open`. Schedule finite local work now. A whole-tree gate remains a spirit pass rather than a CLI feature. [MEASURED: stable-founding-road.mem:813-818,848-873]

''Deferral flags:'' (1) D1/D2 contract and harness progress while the complete page/port path still waits; (2) D3 flag before default choice is acceptable only because the exact phone/Node experiment gates the choice; keep all width code complete. (3) browser founding identity without card UI; (4) W26 floor release/read path while browser and sibling composers lack the Kahu board; (5) W29 reader verifiers while W14–W16 still resolve signer by caller key; (6) K15 exceptions retained in the seed census after their owner lane lands; (7) carriage steps that stand at format/key level while production session signer and face-scoped storage await later. These all read “a now, b later”; only the measured width and human-held ceremony have real gates.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/plan-three-parallel-slots`>>

!! Plan — three parallel slots

# ''Slot 1, identity spine:'' finish W14–W16 and K15 bonds/Handle authority → Kahu/realm frontier → One Face; own all identity byte files and compose hunks. Re-bake X0 only after these and the engine/custody folds settle.
# ''Slot 2, DreamDOM:'' D2 full port and page transport → D3 glass/spike → D4 actor; own DreamDOM engine, island protocol and page files. D2/D3 overlap only on disjoint recording-document/port versus glass-adapter files; one owner per composer hunk.
# ''Slot 3, completion sweep:'' W29 ceremony UI, D0/D1/D5 conformance and D6 sinks, plus G/receipt/ledger/ground tasks; own browser UI, tests, conformance and CLI/SSR/MCP files. Never touch Slot 1 identity modules or Slot 2 port/composer files concurrently. Merge dependency-complete lanes before a shared composer edit; no global-now assumption.

''Critical path to X0:'' fold engine + custody seal → Kahu charter and realm signer/frontier → W14→W15→W16 plus K15 face/Handle bonds → One Face and sealed-store face scope → all identity-byte changes commit → X0 genesis bake and parity → post-bake non-identity closure/UI/proofs → final operator release signing. Ceremony only after the final overview/aftermath loop: D0–D7 surface completeness and width record; all open train rows and census exceptions burned; floor and Kahu readers converge; whole-tree, browser, two-machine runbook and fresh-start walk ready; publication packets prepared; then operator's device/credential gates and two humans execute. This directly answers the ruling: no contextual “finish a now, b later” survives merely because a roadmap labels it afterward.

''Evidence key:'' MEASURED marks the cited carrier's explicit as-built/owed statement; LEAD marks my dependency and classification judgment. Prompt-supplied in-flight W14–W16/I1 and operator ruling count as leads unless the cited carrier independently records them. No repo writes or suites performed.

